Error: Jet.ConstructorReturnsOtherType: `Celsius.new` returns `Float`, not a `Celsius`
  --> Tests/UI/constructor_wrong_owner.jet:6:32
    |
  6 |     new: fn(degrees: Float) -> Float { degrees }
    |                                ^^^^^
 Why: A type's static `new` is its constructor, and a call `Celsius.new(…)` reads as making a `Celsius`, so any other result misleads every caller
 Fix: Make `new` return `Celsius`, `Celsius?` or `Celsius` with a failure contract, or rename the function to say what it returns
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ConstructorReturnsOtherType

Error: Jet.ConstructorReturnsOtherType: `Light.new` returns `Int`, not a `Light`
  --> Tests/UI/constructor_wrong_owner.jet:13:28
    |
 13 |     new: fn(level: Int) -> Int { level }
    |                            ^^^
 Why: A type's static `new` is its constructor, and a call `Light.new(…)` reads as making a `Light`, so any other result misleads every caller
 Fix: Make `new` return `Light`, `Light?` or `Light` with a failure contract, or rename the function to say what it returns
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ConstructorReturnsOtherType
